cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis or its method, please cite it as below, and cite the MetroPT-3 dataset separately."
title: "MetroPT Reliability Agent: a life table for a repairable air production unit"
abstract: >-
  A reliability analysis of the MetroPT-3 dataset, readings from the Air Production
  Unit of a Metro do Porto train. Four documented air-leak failures on one repairable
  unit are treated as a point process rather than as independent lifetimes, on an
  operating-time clock derived from the logging record: the gaps are shown to be the
  machine off, not lost telemetry, which moves the failure rate by 22%. No trend is
  detectable (Laplace U = +0.49; bias-corrected Crow-AMSAA shape 1.26, 90% interval
  0.57 to 3.26), so the reportable result is a rate with an interval and an explicit
  negative. The load-cycle indicator anticipates one of the four reports clearly, once
  ten acquisition freezes are masked; unmasked, a stuck digital channel fabricates 63
  load cycles per hour and outranks every real event, an error this repository made,
  had caught by an agent reading its own tools, and documents rather than quietly fixed.
